#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:4
msgid "ソフトモードと構造相転移"
msgstr "Soft Modes and Structural Phase Transitions"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:6
msgid ""
"高温で対称性の高い結晶が、冷やすと原子配置のわずかなずれによって対称性の低い構造へ移ることがある。 "
"このような構造相転移の多くでは、特定の格子振動の振動数が転移温度に近づくにつれて下がり、 その振動の変位パターンが低温相で凍結する。この振動を "
"**ソフトモード** と呼ぶ。本稿では、 ソフトモードの振幅を秩序変数とみなしてエネルギーを展開し、二重井戸ポテンシャルの形、 "
"その評価法、相転移の型を導く。例として、極性のソフトモードをもつBaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ と、 "
"極性をもたない八面体回転のソフトモードをもつSrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ を取り上げる。"
msgstr ""
"A crystal with high symmetry at high temperature can transform on cooling"
" into a lower-symmetry structure as the atoms shift slightly. In many "
"such structural phase transitions, the frequency of a particular lattice "
"vibration decreases as the transition temperature approaches, and its "
"displacement pattern becomes frozen in the low-temperature phase. This "
"vibration is called a **soft mode**. We expand the energy in the soft-"
"mode amplitude as an order parameter. The expansion gives the shape of "
"the double-well potential, a way to evaluate it, and the types of phase "
"transitions. Our examples are BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , with a polar soft "
"mode, and SrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , with a nonpolar soft mode involving "
"octahedral rotation."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:13
msgid ""
"**前提知識**: :ref:`調和近似とフォノン<phonon>`\\ （とくに\\ :ref:`虚数振動数<imaginary-"
"frequency>`）、:ref:`非調和性<anharmonicity>`、:ref:`反転対称性と自発分極<inversion-and-"
"polarization>`。"
msgstr ""
"**Prerequisites**: :ref:`Harmonic Approximation and Phonons <phonon>`\\  "
"(especially \\ :ref:`Imaginary Frequencies <imaginary-frequency>`), "
":ref:`Anharmonicity <anharmonicity>`, and :ref:`Inversion Symmetry and "
"Spontaneous Polarization <inversion-and-polarization>`."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:15
msgid "**学習目標**:"
msgstr "**Learning objectives**:"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:17
msgid "ソフトモードの考え方と、虚数振動数・低温相の構造との関係を説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain the soft-mode concept and its relation to imaginary frequencies "
"and the structure of the low-temperature phase."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:18
msgid "モードの振幅でエネルギーを展開し、二重井戸の極小の位置と深さを導く。"
msgstr ""
"Expand the energy in the mode amplitude and derive the positions and "
"depth of the minima of a double well."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:19
msgid "反転対称性から :math:`+Q` と :math:`-Q` の極小が等価になる理由を説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain why inversion symmetry makes the minima at :math:`+Q` and "
":math:`-Q` equivalent."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:20
msgid "固有ベクトルに沿ってエネルギーを計算する方法（frozen phonon）の手順と注意点を説明する。"
msgstr ""
"Explain the procedure and precautions for calculating the energy along an"
" eigenvector (the frozen phonon method)."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:21
msgid "変位型と秩序–無秩序型の相転移を、井戸の深さと熱エネルギーの比で区別する。"
msgstr ""
"Distinguish displacive and order–disorder phase transitions by the ratio "
"of the well depth to the thermal energy."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:22
msgid "ソフトモードが強誘電性に限らず、極性をもたない構造変化にも現れることを例で示す。"
msgstr ""
"Use examples to show that soft modes occur in nonpolar structural changes"
" as well as in ferroelectricity."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:27
msgid "ソフトモードの考え方"
msgstr "The Soft-Mode Concept"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:29
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Cochranは、変位による構造相転移を格子振動の不安定性として説明した [Cochran1959]_ [Cochran1960]_。 "
"高温相のある振動モードの振動数 :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}` が、温度 :math:`T` を下げると小さくなり、 "
"そのモードの変位パターンが低温相で凍結する。高温相で振動数の2乗が"
msgstr ""
"Cochran explained structural phase transitions driven by displacements in"
" terms of an instability of lattice vibrations [Cochran1959]_ "
"[Cochran1960]_. A vibrational mode in the high-temperature phase has a "
"frequency :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}` that decreases as the temperature "
":math:`T` is lowered, and its displacement pattern becomes frozen in the "
"low-temperature phase. In the high-temperature phase the squared "
"frequency follows the relation"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:33
#, python-brace-format
msgid "\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2\\propto T-T_0"
msgstr "\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2\\propto T-T_0"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:38
msgid ""
"に従うことを、Cochranの法則と呼ぶ。:math:`T_0` は、高温相での振動数を低温側へ外挿して0になる温度である。 "
"ソフトモードの振動数が温度とともに下がる様子は、中性子の非弾性散乱やRaman散乱で 観測されてきた [Scott1974]_。"
msgstr ""
"This relation is known as Cochran’s law. Here :math:`T_0` is the "
"temperature at which extrapolation of the high-temperature frequency "
"toward lower temperatures reaches zero. The decrease in soft-mode "
"frequency with decreasing temperature has been observed by inelastic "
"neutron scattering and Raman scattering [Scott1974]_."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:42
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`T_0` は転移温度 :math:`T_{\\mathrm c}` "
"と同じとは限らない。転移が連続的に起こる理想的な場合（2次転移）は、 :math:`T_0` "
"で復元力が消え、モードの変位がそこから育つので、:math:`T_{\\mathrm c}=T_0` である。 BaTiO\\ "
":sub:`3`\\ の立方晶–正方晶転移 [Merz1953]_ のような1次転移では、温度が :math:`T_0` に下がる前に、 "
"変位した構造の自由エネルギーが高温相と等しくなる。そのため :math:`T_0<T_{\\mathrm c}` "
"で、:math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}` は :math:`T_{\\mathrm c}` "
"で有限のまま転移が起こる。:math:`T_{\\mathrm c}-T_0` は、\\ :ref:`Landau理論<first-order-"
"transition>`\\ で自由エネルギーの展開から導く。"
msgstr ""
":math:`T_0` need not equal the transition temperature :math:`T_{\\mathrm "
"c}`. In the ideal case of a continuous transition (a second-order "
"transition), the restoring force vanishes at :math:`T_0` and the mode "
"displacement grows from that point, so :math:`T_{\\mathrm c}=T_0`. In a "
"first-order transition such as the cubic-to-tetragonal transition in "
"BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\  (see [Merz1953]_), the free energy of the displaced "
"structure equals that of the high-temperature phase before the "
"temperature reaches :math:`T_0`. Thus :math:`T_0<T_{\\mathrm c}`, and the"
" transition takes place with :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}` still finite at"
" :math:`T_{\\mathrm c}`. We derive :math:`T_{\\mathrm c}-T_0` from the "
"free-energy expansion in \\ :ref:`Landau theory <first-order-"
"transition>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:48
msgid ""
"0 Kの調和近似で高温相の構造のフォノンを計算したとき、ソフトモードが :ref:`虚数振動数<imaginary-frequency>`\\ "
"として現れるのは、その計算条件（\\ :ref:`交換相関汎関数<exchange-correlation-"
"functional>`、格子定数など）で 高温相の構造が不安定な場合である。立方晶BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ はこの例にあたる "
"[CohenKrakauer1990]_。 計算条件で高温相が安定なら、ソフトモードも実数の振動数をもつ。0 Kの計算で虚数になるモードが "
"高温で実数になるのは、大きな振幅の熱振動が\\ :ref:`非調和項<anharmonicity>`\\ "
"を通じて平均的な復元力を変えるためである。"
msgstr ""
"When calculating phonons of the high-temperature structure in the "
"harmonic approximation at 0 K, the soft mode appears as an "
":ref:`imaginary frequency <imaginary-frequency>`\\  if the high-"
"temperature structure is unstable under the chosen calculation conditions"
" (the \\ :ref:`exchange-correlation functional <exchange-correlation-"
"functional>`, lattice constant, and so on). Cubic BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\  is "
"one example [CohenKrakauer1990]_. If the high-temperature structure is "
"stable under the calculation conditions, its soft mode has a real "
"frequency. A mode with an imaginary frequency at 0 K has a real frequency"
" at high temperature because large-amplitude thermal vibrations change "
"the average restoring force through \\ :ref:`anharmonic terms "
"<anharmonicity>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:54
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"ソフトモードの波数 :math:`\\boldsymbol k` によって、低温相の単位胞が決まる。格子ベクトル "
":math:`\\boldsymbol R` だけ離れた胞の変位には 位相因子 :math:`e^{i\\boldsymbol "
"k\\cdot\\boldsymbol R}` が掛かる（\\ :ref:`基準振動とフォノン<ph-normal-"
"modes>`）。Γ点のモードなら、すべての単位胞で 同じ変位が凍結するので、低温相の単位胞は高温相と同じ大きさで、胞内の原子配置だけが変わる。 "
"Γ点以外のモードが凍結すると、波数が逆格子ベクトルの有理数倍なら、単位胞が整数倍に大きくなる。:math:`\\boldsymbol "
"k\\cdot\\boldsymbol R` が :math:`\\pi` の奇数倍になる並進 "
"（1次元鎖のゾーン境界、立方晶のX・M・R点）では、その並進で移った胞の変位が逆向きになる。1次元鎖の\\ :ref:`Peierls不安定性"
"<peierls-instability>`\\ も、周期が2倍になる変形という点で同じ形をしている。"
msgstr ""
"The soft-mode wavevector :math:`\\boldsymbol k` determines the unit cell "
"of the low-temperature phase. The displacement in a cell separated by the"
" lattice vector :math:`\\boldsymbol R` is multiplied by the phase factor "
":math:`e^{i\\boldsymbol k\\cdot\\boldsymbol R}` (see \\ :ref:`normal "
"modes and phonons <ph-normal-modes>`). For a Γ-point mode, the same "
"displacement becomes frozen in every unit cell. The low-temperature cell "
"is the same size as the high-temperature cell, and only the arrangement "
"of atoms within it changes. If a mode away from the Γ point freezes in "
"and the wavevector is a rational multiple of a reciprocal lattice vector,"
" the unit cell grows by an integer factor. For translations with "
":math:`\\boldsymbol k\\cdot\\boldsymbol R` an odd multiple of "
":math:`\\pi` (at the zone boundary of a one-dimensional chain and at X, "
"M, and R in a cubic crystal), the displacement is reversed in the "
"translated cell. The \\ :ref:`Peierls instability <peierls-"
"instability>`\\  in a one-dimensional chain also produces a distortion "
"with twice the original period."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:62
msgid ""
"Γ点のモードのうち、正負のイオンが逆向きに動いて電気双極子モーメントを生むものを **極性ソフトモード** "
"と呼ぶ。これが凍結すると、結晶全体に\\ :ref:`自発分極<spontaneous-polarization>`\\ が生じる。 "
"極性モードが一つの場合、静的な誘電率 :math:`\\varepsilon(0)` と高周波の誘電率 "
":math:`\\varepsilon(\\infty)` の比は、 横波と縦波の光学モードの振動数 "
":math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm{TO}}`、:math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm{LO}}` を使って"
msgstr ""
"A Γ-point mode in which positive and negative ions move in opposite "
"directions and generate an electric dipole moment is called a **polar "
"soft mode**. When it freezes in, a \\ :ref:`spontaneous polarization "
"<spontaneous-polarization>`\\  develops throughout the crystal. If there "
"is one polar mode, the ratio of the static permittivity "
":math:`\\varepsilon(0)` to the high-frequency permittivity "
":math:`\\varepsilon(\\infty)` is expressed in terms of the transverse and"
" longitudinal optical frequencies :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm{TO}}` and "
":math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm{LO}}` as"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:67
msgid "\\frac{\\varepsilon(0)}{\\varepsilon(\\infty)}=\\frac{\\omega_{\\mathrm{LO}}^2}{\\omega_{\\mathrm{TO}}^2}"
msgstr "\\frac{\\varepsilon(0)}{\\varepsilon(\\infty)}=\\frac{\\omega_{\\mathrm{LO}}^2}{\\omega_{\\mathrm{TO}}^2}"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:72
msgid ""
"と表される（Lyddane–Sachs–Tellerの関係） [LST1941]_。ソフトモードが横波の光学モードなら、 "
":math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm{TO}}\\to0` で :math:`\\varepsilon(0)` が発散する。:eq"
":`sm-cochran` を代入すると :math:`\\varepsilon(0)\\propto1/(T-T_0)` "
"となり、強誘電体の誘電率が転移温度の上で従う\\ :ref:`Curie–Weissの法則<paraelectric-phase>`\\ "
"が導かれる [Cochran1960]_。 :math:`T_0` は、Curie–Weissの法則 :eq:`fe-curie-weiss` "
"のCurie–Weiss温度にあたる。1次転移では、誘電率も :math:`T_{\\mathrm c}` で有限のまま転移する。"
msgstr ""
"This is the Lyddane–Sachs–Teller relation [LST1941]_. If the soft mode is"
" transverse optical, then as :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm{TO}}\\to0`, "
":math:`\\varepsilon(0)` diverges. Substituting Equation :eq:`sm-cochran` "
"gives :math:`\\varepsilon(0)\\propto1/(T-T_0)`, yielding the \\ "
":ref:`Curie–Weiss law <paraelectric-phase>`\\  that the permittivity of a"
" ferroelectric obeys above the transition temperature [Cochran1960]_. "
"Here :math:`T_0` is the Curie–Weiss temperature in the Curie–Weiss law "
"(Equation :eq:`fe-curie-weiss`). In a first-order transition the "
"permittivity also remains finite at :math:`T_{\\mathrm c}`."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:80
msgid "秩序変数としてのモードの振幅"
msgstr "Mode Amplitude as an Order Parameter"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:82
msgid ""
"ソフトモードの振幅を :math:`Q` とする。:eq:`ph-mode-energy` と同じく、:ref:`動的行列<dynamical-"
"matrix>`\\ の規格化した実の固有ベクトル :math:`\\boldsymbol e`\\ （:math:`3n` "
"成分）を使い、胞内の原子の変位を並べたベクトル :math:`\\boldsymbol u` と :math:`Q` を"
msgstr ""
"Let :math:`Q` be the soft-mode amplitude. As in Equation :eq:`ph-mode-"
"energy`, use the normalized real eigenvector of the :ref:`dynamical "
"matrix <dynamical-matrix>`\\ , :math:`\\boldsymbol e`\\  (with :math:`3n`"
" components). The vector :math:`\\boldsymbol u`, which collects the "
"atomic displacements within the cell, is related to :math:`Q` by"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:85
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\boldsymbol u=Q\\,M^{-1/2}\\boldsymbol e,\\qquad Q=\\boldsymbol "
"e^{\\mathsf T}M^{1/2}\\boldsymbol u"
msgstr ""
"\\boldsymbol u=Q\\,M^{-1/2}\\boldsymbol e,\\qquad Q=\\boldsymbol "
"e^{\\mathsf T}M^{1/2}\\boldsymbol u"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:90
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"で結ぶ。:math:`M` は各原子の質量 :math:`m_\\kappa` を対角に並べた :math:`3n\\times3n` "
"の行列である。:math:`\\boldsymbol e` は質量の平方根で重み付けた 座標での向きなので、質量の異なる原子では、変位 "
":math:`\\boldsymbol u` の成分の比が :math:`\\boldsymbol e` の成分の比と異なる。 第2式は "
":math:`M^{1/2}\\boldsymbol u` を :math:`\\boldsymbol e` "
"へ射影したもので、:math:`\\boldsymbol u` がこのモードだけからなるとき第1式の逆になる。 "
"ゾーン境界のモードでも、:math:`\\boldsymbol k` と :math:`-\\boldsymbol k` "
"のモードを組み合わせた実のベクトルを使えば同じ形になる。"
msgstr ""
"Here :math:`M` has the atomic masses :math:`m_\\kappa` along its diagonal"
" and has dimensions :math:`3n\\times3n`. Because :math:`\\boldsymbol e` "
"gives a direction in coordinates weighted by the square root of the mass,"
" the ratios of the components of :math:`\\boldsymbol u` differ from those"
" of :math:`\\boldsymbol e` if the atoms have different masses. The second"
" relation projects :math:`M^{1/2}\\boldsymbol u` onto :math:`\\boldsymbol"
" e`. It is the inverse of the first when :math:`\\boldsymbol u` consists "
"of this mode alone. The same form holds for a zone-boundary mode if we "
"use a real vector formed by combining modes at :math:`\\boldsymbol k` and"
" :math:`-\\boldsymbol k`."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:95
msgid ""
"高温相では :math:`Q=0`、低温相では :math:`Q\\ne0` なので、:math:`Q` は相を区別する **秩序変数** "
"の役割をもつ。高温相の構造のまわりで単位胞あたりのエネルギーを :math:`Q` で展開すると"
msgstr ""
"The high-temperature phase has :math:`Q=0` and the low-temperature phase "
"has :math:`Q\\ne0`, so :math:`Q` serves as an **order parameter** that "
"distinguishes the phases. Expanding the energy per unit cell about the "
"high-temperature structure in powers of :math:`Q` gives"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:98
msgid "E(Q)=E_0+\\frac12\\kappa\\,Q^2+\\frac14\\beta\\,Q^4+O(Q^6)"
msgstr "E(Q)=E_0+\\frac12\\kappa\\,Q^2+\\frac14\\beta\\,Q^4+O(Q^6)"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:103
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"と書ける。:math:`\\kappa` は :eq:`ph-mode-energy` の :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm "
"s}^2` に等しい。奇数次の項がないのは、:ref:`+Qと−Qの等価性<sm-inversion-equivalence>`\\ "
"による。:math:`\\beta>0` とする。"
msgstr ""
"The coefficient :math:`\\kappa` equals the squared frequency in Equation "
":eq:`ph-mode-energy`, :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2`. The odd-order terms"
" vanish because of the :ref:`equivalence of +Q and −Q <sm-inversion-"
"equivalence>`\\ . Assume :math:`\\beta>0`."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:105
msgid ""
":math:`\\kappa>0` なら極小は :math:`Q=0` だけで、高温相の構造が安定である。:math:`\\kappa<0` "
"（虚数振動数）なら、:math:`dE/dQ=\\kappa Q+\\beta Q^3=0` の :math:`Q\\ne0` の解として"
msgstr ""
"If :math:`\\kappa>0`, the only minimum is at :math:`Q=0` and the high-"
"temperature structure is stable. If :math:`\\kappa<0` (an imaginary "
"frequency), solving :math:`dE/dQ=\\kappa Q+\\beta Q^3=0` for "
":math:`Q\\ne0` gives minima at"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:108
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Q_0=\\pm\\sqrt{-\\kappa/\\beta}"
msgstr "Q_0=\\pm\\sqrt{-\\kappa/\\beta}"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:113
msgid "に極小が現れる。:eq:`sm-landau` に代入すると、極小の :math:`Q=0` から測った深さは"
msgstr ""
"Substituting these positions into Equation :eq:`sm-landau` gives the "
"depth of the minima measured from :math:`Q=0`:"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:115
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\\Delta "
"E=E(Q_0)-E(0)=\\frac12\\kappa\\left(-\\frac{\\kappa}{\\beta}\\right)+\\frac14\\beta\\left(\\frac{\\kappa}{\\beta}\\right)^2"
"\n"
"=-\\frac{\\kappa^2}{4\\beta}"
msgstr ""
"\\Delta "
"E=E(Q_0)-E(0)=\\frac12\\kappa\\left(-\\frac{\\kappa}{\\beta}\\right)+\\frac14\\beta\\left(\\frac{\\kappa}{\\beta}\\right)^2"
"\n"
"=-\\frac{\\kappa^2}{4\\beta}"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:121
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"である。極小での曲率は :math:`E''(Q_0)=\\kappa+3\\beta Q_0^2=-2\\kappa>0` で、低温相の構造は "
"このモードに沿って安定である。この模型では、低温相でのモードの振動数は "
":math:`\\sqrt{-2\\kappa}`、つまり高温相の虚数振動数の大きさの :math:`\\sqrt2` 倍になる。"
msgstr ""
"The curvature at a minimum is :math:`E''(Q_0)=\\kappa+3\\beta "
"Q_0^2=-2\\kappa>0`, so the low-temperature structure is stable along this"
" mode. In this model, the mode frequency in the low-temperature phase is "
":math:`\\sqrt{-2\\kappa}`, or :math:`\\sqrt2` times the magnitude of the "
"imaginary frequency in the high-temperature phase."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:125
msgid ":numref:`fig-soft-mode-double-well` に、この二重井戸と、2次の項だけの放物線を示す。"
msgstr ""
":numref:`fig-soft-mode-double-well` shows the double well and the "
"parabola obtained by keeping only the quadratic term."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:127
msgid "二重井戸のエネルギー曲線と、原点で負の曲率をもつ放物線。極小はマイナスQ0とQ0にあり、深さをΔEで示す。"
msgstr ""
"Energy curve of a double well and a parabola of negative curvature at the"
" origin. The minima are at −Q0 and Q0, and ΔE indicates the depth."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:133
msgid ""
":math:`\\kappa<0`、:math:`\\beta>0` の式 :eq:`sm-landau`\\ "
"（青の実線）と、その2次の項だけの放物線 :math:`\\kappa Q^2/2`\\ （赤の破線）。点は極小 :math:`\\pm "
"Q_0`\\ （式 :eq:`sm-q0`）、両矢印は深さ :math:`\\Delta E`\\ （式 :eq:`sm-"
"depth`）。係数は説明用で、特定の物質の値ではない。"
msgstr ""
"For :math:`\\kappa<0` and :math:`\\beta>0`, the solid blue curve shows "
"Equation :eq:`sm-landau`\\ , and the dashed red curve shows the parabola "
":math:`\\kappa Q^2/2`\\  from its quadratic term alone. The dots mark the"
" minima :math:`\\pm Q_0`\\  (Equation :eq:`sm-q0`) and the double-headed "
"arrow shows the depth :math:`\\Delta E`\\  (Equation :eq:`sm-depth`). The"
" coefficients are illustrative and do not represent any particular "
"material."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:137
msgid ""
"ここまでは0 Kのエネルギーである。温度の効果は、:eq:`sm-landau` を自由エネルギーと読み替え、:math:`\\kappa` が "
":math:`\\kappa=\\Omega a(T-T_0)`\\ （:math:`\\Omega` は単位胞の体積、:math:`a` "
"は単位体積あたりの自由エネルギーの係数）と 温度とともに変わるとする\\ :ref:`Landau理論<landau-theory>`\\ "
"で取り込む。この仮定から、 ソフトモードの振動数が :eq:`sm-cochran` "
"に従って下がることと、2次転移と1次転移の違いが導かれる。BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の 三つの転移は、いずれも1次転移である "
"[Zhong1995]_。"
msgstr ""
"So far the energy has been evaluated at 0 K. To account for temperature, "
"we interpret Equation :eq:`sm-landau` as a free energy and take "
":math:`\\kappa` to vary with temperature as :math:`\\kappa=\\Omega "
"a(T-T_0)`\\  (:math:`\\Omega` is the unit-cell volume and :math:`a` is "
"the coefficient for free energy per unit volume), as in \\ :ref:`Landau "
"theory <landau-theory>`\\ . This assumption gives the decrease in soft-"
"mode frequency described by Equation :eq:`sm-cochran` and explains the "
"difference between a second-order transition and a first-order "
"transition. All three transitions in BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\  are first-order "
"transitions [Zhong1995]_."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:146
msgid "+Qと−Qの等価性と反転対称性"
msgstr "Equivalence of +Q and −Q and Inversion Symmetry"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:148
msgid ""
"高温相の構造に、変位パターンを :math:`\\boldsymbol e\\to-\\boldsymbol e` に写す対称操作があるとする。 "
"対称操作で移り合う構造はエネルギーが等しいので :math:`E(Q)=E(-Q)` が成り立ち、 :eq:`sm-landau` "
"の奇数次の項は消える。このとき :math:`+Q_0` と :math:`-Q_0` の極小は等価で、深さも等しい。"
msgstr ""
"Suppose the high-temperature structure has a symmetry operation that maps"
" the displacement pattern as :math:`\\boldsymbol e\\to-\\boldsymbol e`. "
"Structures related by a symmetry operation have equal energies, so "
":math:`E(Q)=E(-Q)` and the odd-order terms in Equation :eq:`sm-landau` "
"vanish. The minima at :math:`+Q_0` and :math:`-Q_0` are then equivalent "
"and have the same depth."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:152
msgid ""
"極性ソフトモードでは、この操作は反転である。立方晶ペロブスカイトの反転中心にBサイトの原子を置くと、 "
"反転は各副格子を同じ副格子へ写し、各原子の変位の向きを逆にする。全原子が同じパターンで動くΓ点の 極性モードでは、反転によって :math:`Q`"
" が :math:`-Q` に変わる。\\ :ref:`自発分極は反転で符号を変える<inversion-and-polarization>`\\"
" ので、 二つの極小は大きさが等しく向きが反対の分極をもつ。結晶の中で異なる極小を選んだ領域（:ref:`分域<ferroelectric-"
"domains>`）が共存しうるのも、 この等価性による。"
msgstr ""
"For a polar soft mode, the operation is inversion. With a B-site atom at "
"the inversion center of a cubic perovskite, inversion maps each "
"sublattice onto itself and reverses each atom's displacement. For a polar"
" Γ-point mode, in which all atoms follow the same displacement pattern, "
"inversion changes :math:`Q` to :math:`-Q`. Because \\ :ref:`spontaneous "
"polarization reverses sign under inversion <inversion-and-"
"polarization>`\\ , the minima have polarizations of equal magnitude and "
"opposite direction. This equivalence also allows regions of a crystal "
"that select different minima (:ref:`domains <ferroelectric-domains>`) to "
"coexist."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:158
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"ゾーン境界のモードでは、高温相の格子並進が同じ役割をもつことがある。格子ベクトル :math:`\\boldsymbol R` "
"の並進は変位に位相因子 :math:`e^{i\\boldsymbol k\\cdot\\boldsymbol R}` "
"を掛けるので、:math:`\\boldsymbol k\\cdot\\boldsymbol R` が :math:`\\pi` の奇数倍になる "
":math:`\\boldsymbol R` があれば "
"（1次元鎖のゾーン境界、立方晶のX・M・R点）、その並進は各胞の変位の符号を逆にし、ずらした構造は :math:`-Q` の構造になる。 このとき"
" :math:`+Q` と :math:`-Q` は、原点の取り方だけが違う同じ構造である。六方格子のK点のように、並進で位相が "
":math:`2\\pi/3` ずつずれる波数では、並進は :math:`Q` を :math:`-Q` へ写さない。:math:`+Q` と "
":math:`-Q` が等価かどうかは、並進以外の対称操作で決まる。"
msgstr ""
"For zone-boundary modes, a lattice translation of the high-temperature "
"phase can play the same role. Translation by a lattice vector "
":math:`\\boldsymbol R` multiplies the displacement by "
":math:`e^{i\\boldsymbol k\\cdot\\boldsymbol R}`. If :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"k\\cdot\\boldsymbol R` is an odd multiple of :math:`\\pi` for some "
":math:`\\boldsymbol R` (as at the zone boundary of a one-dimensional "
"chain or at X, M, and R in a cubic crystal), the translation reverses the"
" displacement in each cell and gives the structure at :math:`-Q`. In that"
" case :math:`+Q` and :math:`-Q` describe the same structure with "
"different choices of origin. At wavevectors such as K in a hexagonal "
"lattice, where translation shifts the phase in steps of :math:`2\\pi/3`, "
"translation does not map :math:`Q` to :math:`-Q`. Other symmetry "
"operations determine whether :math:`+Q` and :math:`-Q` are equivalent."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:164
msgid ""
":math:`\\boldsymbol e\\to-\\boldsymbol e` "
"に写す操作がないモードでは、3次の項は対称性で禁じられず、現れうる。その係数が0でなければ、 :math:`+Q` と :math:`-Q` "
"の極小は等価でない。"
msgstr ""
"For a mode without a symmetry operation of the form :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"e\\to-\\boldsymbol e`, symmetry does not forbid a cubic term, so one may "
"appear. If its coefficient is nonzero, the minima at :math:`+Q` and "
":math:`-Q` are inequivalent."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:170
msgid "二重井戸ポテンシャル"
msgstr "Double-Well Potential"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:172
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
":math:`\\kappa<0` の :eq:`sm-landau` のように、対称な位置 :math:`Q=0` "
"の山を挟んで等価な二つの極小をもつ エネルギー曲線を **二重井戸ポテンシャル** と呼ぶ。曲線の形は二つの部分で決まる。 "
"小さい変位の領域では、2次の項 :math:`\\kappa Q^2/2` が支配し、曲率 :math:`\\kappa` "
"はフォノン計算の振動数の2乗 :math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2` と同じ量で、虚数振動数のときは負になる。 "
"大きい変位の領域では、4次以上の非調和項がエネルギーを押し上げ、井戸の外側の壁を作る。"
msgstr ""
"In the :math:`\\kappa<0` case of Equation :eq:`sm-landau`, the energy "
"curve has two equivalent minima separated by a peak at the symmetric "
"position :math:`Q=0`. Such a curve is called a **double-well potential**."
" Two contributions determine its shape. At small displacements, the "
"quadratic term :math:`\\kappa Q^2/2` dominates, and the curvature "
":math:`\\kappa` is the same quantity as the squared frequency "
":math:`\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2` in a phonon calculation, which is negative"
" for an imaginary frequency. At large displacements, quartic and higher-"
"order anharmonic terms raise the energy and form the outer walls of the "
"wells."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:177
msgid ""
":eq:`sm-q0` と :eq:`sm-depth` が示すように、極小の位置と深さは :math:`\\kappa` と "
":math:`\\beta` の両方で決まる。 同じ曲率 :math:`\\kappa` でも、壁の立ち上がり :math:`\\beta` "
"が半分なら、:math:`Q_0` は :math:`\\sqrt2` 倍、:math:`\\Delta E` "
"は2倍になる。したがって、計算手法や模型を比べるときは、原点の曲率と大きい変位での壁を別々に "
"比べる必要がある。片方が合っていても、もう片方が合うとは限らない。"
msgstr ""
"As Equations :eq:`sm-q0` and :eq:`sm-depth` show, the positions and "
"depths of the minima depend on both :math:`\\kappa` and :math:`\\beta`. "
"Even with the same curvature :math:`\\kappa`, cutting the wall "
"coefficient :math:`\\beta` in half scales :math:`Q_0` by a factor of "
":math:`\\sqrt2` and doubles :math:`\\Delta E`. Therefore, when comparing "
"methods or models, compare the curvature at the origin and the walls at "
"large displacements separately. Agreement in one does not guarantee "
"agreement in the other."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:182
msgid ""
"井戸の深さは、格子のひずみとの結合でも変わる。ひずみ :math:`\\eta` と弾性定数 :math:`C_{\\mathrm{el}}` "
"を使い、 対称性から許される最低次の結合 :math:`\\lambda\\eta Q^2` を加えると"
msgstr ""
"Coupling to lattice strain also changes the well depth. Using strain "
":math:`\\eta` and elastic constant :math:`C_{\\mathrm{el}}` and adding "
"the lowest-order coupling allowed by symmetry, :math:`\\lambda\\eta Q^2`,"
" gives"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:185
msgid "E(Q,\\eta)=\\frac12\\kappa\\,Q^2+\\frac14\\beta\\,Q^4+\\lambda\\,\\eta\\,Q^2+\\frac12C_{\\mathrm{el}}\\,\\eta^2"
msgstr "E(Q,\\eta)=\\frac12\\kappa\\,Q^2+\\frac14\\beta\\,Q^4+\\lambda\\,\\eta\\,Q^2+\\frac12C_{\\mathrm{el}}\\,\\eta^2"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:190
msgid ""
"となる。ひずみを固定すると、2次の係数は "
":math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{eff}}=\\kappa+2\\lambda\\eta` に変わり、 "
":math:`\\lambda\\eta<0` の向きのひずみは井戸を深くする。ひずみも緩和させると、:math:`\\partial "
"E/\\partial\\eta=0` から :math:`\\eta=-\\lambda Q^2/C_{\\mathrm{el}}` "
"で、代入すると4次の係数が"
msgstr ""
"At fixed strain the quadratic coefficient becomes "
":math:`\\kappa_{\\mathrm{eff}}=\\kappa+2\\lambda\\eta`, and a strain with"
" :math:`\\lambda\\eta<0` deepens the well. If the strain is allowed to "
"relax as well, :math:`\\partial E/\\partial\\eta=0` gives "
":math:`\\eta=-\\lambda Q^2/C_{\\mathrm{el}}`. Substituting this back "
"reduces the quartic coefficient to"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:194
msgid "\\beta_{\\mathrm{eff}}=\\beta-\\frac{2\\lambda^2}{C_{\\mathrm{el}}}"
msgstr "\\beta_{\\mathrm{eff}}=\\beta-\\frac{2\\lambda^2}{C_{\\mathrm{el}}}"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:199
msgid ""
"に下がる。ひずみとの結合は壁を低くし、井戸を深くする。:math:`\\beta_{\\mathrm{eff}}<0` になれば、 \\ "
":ref:`1次転移<first-order-transition>`\\ になる。体積も同じように :math:`\\kappa` "
"を変えるので、二重井戸の深さは 計算に使う格子定数に敏感である。"
msgstr ""
"Coupling to strain lowers the walls and deepens the well. If "
":math:`\\beta_{\\mathrm{eff}}<0`, the result is a \\ :ref:`first-order "
"transition <first-order-transition>`\\ . Volume also changes "
":math:`\\kappa`, so the depth of the double well is sensitive to the "
"lattice constant used in the calculation."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:203
msgid ""
"ソフトモードが縮退している場合、秩序変数はベクトルになる。立方晶の結晶のΓ点の極性モードは、 :math:`x,y,z` "
"の3方向に縮退している。振幅を :math:`\\boldsymbol Q=(Q_x,Q_y,Q_z)` "
"とすると、立方晶の対称性が許す4次までの項は"
msgstr ""
"If the soft mode is degenerate, the order parameter becomes a vector. In "
"a cubic crystal the polar Γ-point mode is degenerate along the three "
"directions :math:`x,y,z`. Writing the amplitude as :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"Q=(Q_x,Q_y,Q_z)`, the terms allowed by cubic symmetry up to fourth order "
"are"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:206
msgid ""
"E(\\boldsymbol Q)=\\frac12\\kappa|\\boldsymbol "
"Q|^2+\\frac14\\beta|\\boldsymbol Q|^4\n"
"+\\frac14\\beta'\\left(Q_x^2Q_y^2+Q_y^2Q_z^2+Q_z^2Q_x^2\\right)"
msgstr ""
"E(\\boldsymbol Q)=\\frac12\\kappa|\\boldsymbol "
"Q|^2+\\frac14\\beta|\\boldsymbol Q|^4\n"
"+\\frac14\\beta'\\left(Q_x^2Q_y^2+Q_y^2Q_z^2+Q_z^2Q_x^2\\right)"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:212
msgid ""
"である [Devonshire1949]_。:math:`|\\boldsymbol Q|` を固定すると、最後の括弧は "
":math:`\\langle001\\rangle` 方向で0、 :math:`\\langle110\\rangle` で "
":math:`|\\boldsymbol Q|^4/4`、:math:`\\langle111\\rangle` で "
":math:`|\\boldsymbol Q|^4/3` となり、 この範囲の最小と最大はそれぞれ "
":math:`\\langle001\\rangle` と :math:`\\langle111\\rangle` である。 したがって "
":math:`\\beta'>0` なら :math:`\\langle001\\rangle` "
"方向（正方晶）、:math:`\\beta'<0` なら :math:`\\langle111\\rangle` 方向 "
"（菱面体晶）に変位する。:math:`\\langle110\\rangle` 方向（直方晶、斜方晶ともいう）が最も低くなるには6次の項が要る。"
msgstr ""
"as given in [Devonshire1949]_. With :math:`|\\boldsymbol Q|` fixed, the "
"expression in the last parentheses is zero along "
":math:`\\langle001\\rangle`. Along :math:`\\langle110\\rangle` it is "
":math:`|\\boldsymbol Q|^4/4`, and along :math:`\\langle111\\rangle` it is"
" :math:`|\\boldsymbol Q|^4/3`. Its minimum and maximum in this range are "
"along :math:`\\langle001\\rangle` and :math:`\\langle111\\rangle`, "
"respectively. Thus if :math:`\\beta'>0` the displacement is along "
":math:`\\langle001\\rangle` (tetragonal), whereas if :math:`\\beta'<0` it"
" is along :math:`\\langle111\\rangle` (rhombohedral). Sixth-order terms "
"are needed for the :math:`\\langle110\\rangle` direction (orthorhombic) "
"to have the lowest energy."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:221
msgid "固有ベクトルに沿ってエネルギーを調べる方法"
msgstr "Exploring the Energy Along an Eigenvector"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:223
msgid ""
"二重井戸の形は、ソフトモードの変位パターンに沿って原子を動かした構造の全エネルギーを、 振幅ごとに計算すれば得られる。この方法を **frozen"
" phonon法** と呼ぶ。小さい振幅での曲率から振動数を読めば、\\ :ref:`力定数を求める方法<phonon-force-"
"constant-calculation>`\\ の一つにもなる。 手順は次のとおりである。"
msgstr ""
"The shape of the double well can be obtained by calculating, for each "
"amplitude, the total energy of a structure whose atoms have been "
"displaced along the soft-mode pattern. This is called the **frozen phonon"
" method**. If the frequency is obtained from the curvature at small "
"amplitudes, this is also one of the \\ :ref:`methods for calculating "
"force constants <phonon-force-constant-calculation>`\\ . The procedure is"
" as follows."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:227
msgid "高温相の構造（例えば立方晶）を用意し、ソフトモードの固有ベクトルを、フォノン計算か文献から得る。"
msgstr ""
"Prepare the high-temperature structure (for example, the cubic phase) and"
" obtain the soft-mode eigenvector from a phonon calculation or the "
"literature."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:228
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"振幅 :math:`Q` を何点か選び、各原子 :math:`\\kappa` を、固有ベクトルの成分を質量の平方根で割った "
":math:`\\boldsymbol e_\\kappa/\\sqrt{m_\\kappa}` に比例する分だけ動かす（:eq:`sm-"
"mode-amplitude`）。固有ベクトルの成分の比のまま "
"動かすと、質量の異なる原子を含む結晶では、変位が目的のモードから外れる。プログラムが質量で割った後の変位を出力する場合は、 その比をそのまま使う。"
msgstr ""
"Choose several amplitudes :math:`Q` and displace each atom "
":math:`\\kappa` by an amount proportional to :math:`\\boldsymbol "
"e_\\kappa/\\sqrt{m_\\kappa}`, its eigenvector component divided by the "
"square root of its mass (Equation :eq:`sm-mode-amplitude`). Using the "
"ratios of the eigenvector components directly would give displacements "
"that deviate from the intended mode in a crystal with unequal atomic "
"masses. If the program outputs displacements after division by the mass "
"factor, use those ratios directly."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:232
msgid ""
"各構造で、原子座標とセルを固定したまま全エネルギーを計算する（\\ :ref:`単点計算<structure-optimization>`）。 "
"構造を緩和させると、原子は指定した変位から別の方向へ動き、:math:`Q` の値が保てない。"
msgstr ""
"For each structure, calculate the total energy with the atomic "
"coordinates and cell fixed (a \\ :ref:`single-point calculation "
"<structure-optimization>`). If the structure is relaxed, the atoms move "
"away from the prescribed displacements and the value of :math:`Q` cannot "
"be maintained."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:234
msgid ""
"同じ体積の :math:`Q=0` を基準に :math:`\\Delta E(Q)=E(Q)-E(0)` を\\ :ref:`化学式単位あたり"
"<energy-reference>`\\ で求め、 :eq:`sm-landau` のような多項式で当てはめる。"
msgstr ""
"Use the structure at :math:`Q=0` and the same volume as the reference, "
"compute the energy difference :math:`\\Delta E(Q)=E(Q)-E(0)` in units of "
"energy \\ :ref:`per formula unit <energy-reference>`\\ , and fit it to a "
"polynomial such as Equation :eq:`sm-landau`."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:237
msgid ""
"Γ点のモードでは、どれか一つの原子を固定してもよい。:math:`\\boldsymbol "
"e_\\kappa/\\sqrt{m_\\kappa}` に比例する変位から、 "
"固定する原子の変位を全原子について一様に引けばよい。全原子の一様な並進はエネルギーを 変えないからである（\\ :ref:`音響和則"
"<harmonic-approximation>`）。実際の計算では、振幅を一つの原子の 変位 :math:`x`\\ "
"（Å）で測り、他の原子の変位をその比 :math:`r_\\kappa` で決めることが多い。ただし、 曲率 "
":math:`k_x=d^2E/dx^2` から振動数を求めるときは、パターンから重心の並進を除く必要がある。 重心の並進を除いた比を "
":math:`\\tilde "
"r_\\kappa=r_\\kappa-\\sum_{\\kappa'}m_{\\kappa'}r_{\\kappa'}/\\sum_{\\kappa'}m_{\\kappa'}`"
" とすると、 :eq:`sm-mode-amplitude` の第2式から基準座標は "
":math:`Q=\\sqrt{M_{\\mathrm{eff}}}\\,x`、"
msgstr ""
"For a Γ-point mode, you may keep one atom fixed. To do so, subtract that "
"atom's displacement from the displacements proportional to "
":math:`\\boldsymbol e_\\kappa/\\sqrt{m_\\kappa}` for all atoms. A uniform"
" translation of all atoms leaves the energy unchanged (see the \\ "
":ref:`acoustic sum rule <harmonic-approximation>`). In practice the "
"amplitude is often measured as the displacement :math:`x`\\  (Å) of one "
"atom, and the displacements of the others are set by the ratios "
":math:`r_\\kappa`. However, to obtain the frequency from the curvature "
":math:`k_x=d^2E/dx^2`, the translation of the center of mass must be "
"removed from the pattern. If :math:`\\tilde "
"r_\\kappa=r_\\kappa-\\sum_{\\kappa'}m_{\\kappa'}r_{\\kappa'}/\\sum_{\\kappa'}m_{\\kappa'}`"
" gives the ratios with the center-of-mass translation removed, the second"
" relation in Equation :eq:`sm-mode-amplitude` gives the normal coordinate"
" :math:`Q=\\sqrt{M_{\\mathrm{eff}}}\\,x`, with"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:245
msgid ""
"M_{\\mathrm{eff}}=\\sum_\\kappa m_\\kappa\\tilde r_\\kappa^2,\\qquad\n"
"\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2=\\frac{k_x}{M_{\\mathrm{eff}}}"
msgstr ""
"M_{\\mathrm{eff}}=\\sum_\\kappa m_\\kappa\\tilde r_\\kappa^2,\\qquad\n"
"\\omega_{\\mathrm s}^2=\\frac{k_x}{M_{\\mathrm{eff}}}"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:251
msgid ""
"となる。一様な並進は位置エネルギーを変えないが、運動エネルギーは変えるからである。 :ref:`1次元二原子鎖<ph-diatomic-"
"chain>`\\ のΓ点の光学モードで確かめると、Bを固定してAだけを :math:`x` 動かす パターンでは、各Aの両側のばねが "
":math:`x` だけ伸び縮みするので :math:`E=Cx^2` で、:math:`k_x=2C` である。 "
":math:`M_{\\mathrm{eff}}` の代わりにAの質量 :math:`m_{\\mathrm A}` を使うと "
":math:`\\omega^2=2C/m_{\\mathrm A}` と誤る。 重心を除くと "
":math:`M_{\\mathrm{eff}}=m_{\\mathrm A}m_{\\mathrm B}/(m_{\\mathrm "
"A}+m_{\\mathrm B})` となり、 :eq:`ph-chain-dispersion` のΓ点の値 "
":math:`2C(1/m_{\\mathrm A}+1/m_{\\mathrm B})` に一致する。 :eq:`sm-mode-"
"amplitude` の第2式で :math:`Q` を求めれば、変位に一様な並進が含まれていても値は変わらない。 光学モードの "
":math:`\\boldsymbol e` は並進の固有ベクトル（成分が :math:`\\sqrt{m_\\kappa}` "
"に比例）と直交するからである。 井戸の深さ :math:`\\Delta E` は位置エネルギーだけで決まるので、この補正を受けない。"
msgstr ""
"This is because a uniform translation leaves the potential energy "
"unchanged but changes the kinetic energy. The Γ-point optical mode in the"
" :ref:`one-dimensional diatomic chain <ph-diatomic-chain>`\\  provides a "
"check. When B is held fixed and only A moves by :math:`x`, the springs on"
" either side of each A stretch or compress by :math:`x`, so "
":math:`E=Cx^2` and :math:`k_x=2C`. Using A's mass in place of "
":math:`M_{\\mathrm{eff}}`, i.e., using :math:`m_{\\mathrm A}`, "
"incorrectly gives :math:`\\omega^2=2C/m_{\\mathrm A}`. Removing the "
"translation of the center of mass gives "
":math:`M_{\\mathrm{eff}}=m_{\\mathrm A}m_{\\mathrm B}/(m_{\\mathrm "
"A}+m_{\\mathrm B})`, which yields the squared frequency at Γ from "
"Equation :eq:`ph-chain-dispersion`, :math:`2C(1/m_{\\mathrm "
"A}+1/m_{\\mathrm B})`. If the second relation in Equation :eq:`sm-mode-"
"amplitude` is used to find :math:`Q`, the value is unchanged even if the "
"displacement includes a uniform translation. This is because "
":math:`\\boldsymbol e` for the optical mode is orthogonal to the "
"translation eigenvector, whose components are proportional to "
":math:`\\sqrt{m_\\kappa}`. Since the well depth :math:`\\Delta E` depends"
" only on potential energy, it is unaffected by this correction."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:261
msgid ""
"frozen phonon法が調べるのは、配置空間の中の一本の直線の上のエネルギーである。他のモードやひずみを "
"緩和させるとエネルギーはさらに下がりうるので、得られる井戸の深さは、すべての自由度を最適化した "
"極小までの深さを超えない。変位が大きくなると、最もエネルギーが下がる変位の比が、小さい変位での 固有ベクトルからずれることもある。"
msgstr ""
"The frozen phonon method samples the energy along a single straight line "
"in configuration space. Allowing other modes and strain to relax can "
"lower the energy further, so the calculated well depth cannot exceed the "
"depth of the minimum obtained by optimizing all degrees of freedom. At "
"large displacements, the displacement ratios that give the largest energy"
" decrease can also differ from those of the small-displacement "
"eigenvector."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:269
msgid "変位型と秩序–無秩序型の相転移"
msgstr "Displacive and Order–Disorder Phase Transitions"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:271
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"二重井戸をもつ結晶の相転移は、単位胞ごとの井戸の深さ :math:`|\\Delta E|` と、隣の胞の変位どうしの "
"相互作用のエネルギーの比で、二つの極限に分けられる [Dove1997]_。転移温度の熱エネルギー :math:`k_{\\mathrm "
"B}T_{\\mathrm c}` は、どちらの極限でも主に胞どうしの相互作用で決まり、井戸の深さそのものでは 決まらない。そのため、この比は "
":math:`|\\Delta E|/k_{\\mathrm B}T_{\\mathrm c}` で見積もれる （:numref:`fig-"
"soft-mode-displacive-order-disorder`）。"
msgstr ""
"Phase transitions in crystals with double wells fall into two limiting "
"cases according to the ratio of the well depth per unit cell, "
":math:`|\\Delta E|`, to the interaction energy between displacements in "
"neighboring cells [Dove1997]_. In both limits the thermal energy at the "
"transition temperature, :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}T_{\\mathrm c}`, is "
"determined mainly by interactions between cells. The well depth alone "
"does not determine it. Thus the ratio can be estimated by :math:`|\\Delta"
" E|/k_{\\mathrm B}T_{\\mathrm c}` (:numref:`fig-soft-mode-displacive-"
"order-disorder`)."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:277
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**変位型** （:math:`|\\Delta E|\\ll k_{\\mathrm B}T_{\\mathrm "
"c}`）では、転移温度の上で原子は二つの井戸を区別せず、 "
"対称な位置のまわりで振動する。各胞の変位の分布は対称な位置を中心に一つの山をもち、各胞にも "
"局所的な変位は残らない。冷やしていくと、隣どうしの強い相互作用のために原子は周りと一緒に "
"同じ向きへずれ、平均位置が少しずつ対称な位置から離れていく。ソフトモードの振動数が0に近づき、 "
"変位が凍結するのがこの型である。不安定な揺らぎは、ブリルアンゾーンのΓ点の近くなど狭い範囲に限られる [Zhong1995]_。"
msgstr ""
"In the **displacive limit** (:math:`|\\Delta E|\\ll k_{\\mathrm "
"B}T_{\\mathrm c}`), above the transition temperature the atoms do not "
"distinguish between the two wells and vibrate about the symmetric "
"position. The displacement distribution in each cell has a single peak "
"centered on the symmetric position, and no local displacement remains "
"within individual cells. On cooling, strong interactions between "
"neighbors cause atoms to shift in the same direction as those around "
"them, and the mean position gradually moves away from the symmetric "
"position. In this type of transition, the soft-mode frequency approaches "
"zero and the displacement freezes in. Unstable fluctuations are confined "
"to a small region, for example near the Γ point in the Brillouin zone "
"[Zhong1995]_."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:284
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"**秩序–無秩序型** （:math:`|\\Delta E|\\gg k_{\\mathrm B}T_{\\mathrm "
"c}`）では、転移温度より十分に高い温度でも、 各胞の原子はどちらかの井戸の底にいて、ときどき反対側へ飛び移る。転移温度の上では、どちらの井戸に "
"いるかが胞ごとにばらばらなので、平均構造は対称でも各胞には局所的な変位が残っている。 "
"変位の分布には二つの山がある。転移は、各胞の井戸の選び方がそろうことで起こり、転移のエントロピーは 主に配置の数から生じる "
"[Dove1997]_。胞ごとにほぼ独立に井戸を選ぶので、揺らぎはブリルアンゾーン全体に 広がる [Zhong1995]_。"
msgstr ""
"In the **order–disorder limit** (:math:`|\\Delta E|\\gg k_{\\mathrm "
"B}T_{\\mathrm c}`), even well above the transition temperature, the atoms"
" in each cell sit at the bottom of one well and occasionally jump to the "
"other. Above the transition temperature, the choice of well varies from "
"cell to cell, so local displacements remain in individual cells even "
"though the average structure is symmetric. The displacement distribution "
"has two peaks. The transition occurs as the cells align their choice of "
"well, and the entropy of the transition comes mainly from the number of "
"configurations [Dove1997]_. Because each cell makes its choice nearly "
"independently, fluctuations spread throughout the Brillouin zone "
"[Zhong1995]_."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:291
msgid "左は浅い二重井戸で、熱エネルギーの線が山より上にあり、二つの井戸を一続きに覆う。右は深い二重井戸で、熱エネルギーの線が山より下にあり、二つの井戸の底だけを別々に覆う。"
msgstr ""
"Left: In the shallow double well, the thermal energy line lies above the "
"barrier and covers both wells in one continuous range. Right: In the deep"
" double well, the line lies below the barrier and covers only the bottoms"
" of the two wells in separate ranges."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:297
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"単位胞あたりのエネルギー曲線（青）と、極小から :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}T` だけ上の高さ（赤の点線）。 "
"赤の太線は、そのエネルギーで原子が届く範囲を示す。左の変位型では二つの井戸にまたがり、 "
"右の秩序–無秩序型では片方の井戸の中に限られる。係数は説明用で、特定の物質の値ではない。"
msgstr ""
"Energy curves per unit cell (blue) and a level :math:`k_{\\mathrm B}T` "
"above the minima (dotted red lines). The thick red segments show the "
"ranges the atoms can reach at that energy. On the left, in the displacive"
" case, the range spans both wells. On the right, in the order–disorder "
"case, the range is confined to one well. The coefficients are "
"illustrative and do not represent any particular material."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:301
msgid ""
"二つの型は極限であり、多くの物質はその間にある。0 Kで計算した井戸の深さだけでは型は決まらず、 "
"胞どうしの相互作用の強さとの比が型を決める。Zhongらは、計算した揺らぎがブリルアンゾーンのどの範囲まで "
"広がっているかを、型を判定する基準に使った [Zhong1995]_。"
msgstr ""
"The two types are limiting cases, and many materials lie between them. "
"The well depth calculated at 0 K alone does not determine the type. What "
"determines it is the ratio of that depth to the strength of the "
"interactions between cells. Zhong and colleagues classified the "
"transitions by how much of the Brillouin zone the calculated fluctuations"
" covered [Zhong1995]_."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:308
msgid "極性をもたないソフトモード：SrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の八面体回転"
msgstr "Nonpolar Soft Mode: Octahedral Rotation in SrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:310
msgid ""
"ソフトモードは強誘電性に限らない。ペロブスカイト型のSrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ は、室温では立方晶である。 約105 "
"K（初期の文献では110 K）で、TiO\\ :sub:`6`\\ "
"八面体が一つの立方晶の軸のまわりに回転した正方晶の構造へ移る。UnokiとSakudoはFe\\ :sup:`3+`\\ "
"の電子スピン共鳴で八面体の回転を見いだし、その回転角を転移の 秩序変数として温度変化を追った "
"[UnokiSakudo1967]_。ShiraneとYamadaは中性子散乱で、立方晶の ブリルアンゾーンの角のR点 "
":math:`(\\pi/a)(1,1,1)` のモードが転移温度に向かって低くなることを観測した "
"[ShiraneYamada1969]_。Fleuryらは、転移温度の下でRaman散乱のソフトモードの振動数が "
"転移温度に向かって0に近づくことを示した [Fleury1968]_。"
msgstr ""
"Soft modes also occur outside ferroelectricity. Perovskite SrTiO\\ "
":sub:`3`\\  is cubic at room temperature. At about 105 K (110 K in the "
"early literature), it transforms into a tetragonal structure in which the"
" TiO\\ :sub:`6`\\  octahedra have rotated about one cubic axis. Using "
"electron spin resonance of Fe\\ :sup:`3+`\\ , Unoki and Sakudo detected "
"the octahedral rotation and tracked the rotation angle with temperature "
"as the order parameter of the transition [UnokiSakudo1967]_. Using "
"neutron scattering, Shirane and Yamada observed softening of the R-point "
"mode, :math:`(\\pi/a)(1,1,1)`, at the corner of the cubic Brillouin zone "
"as the transition temperature is approached [ShiraneYamada1969]_. Fleury "
"and colleagues showed that below the transition temperature, the soft-"
"mode frequency measured by Raman scattering approaches zero as the "
"temperature approaches the transition [Fleury1968]_."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:317
msgid ""
"隣り合う八面体は頂点の酸素を共有しているので、一つの八面体が回ると、同じ面内の隣の八面体は 逆向きに回る（:numref:`fig-soft-"
"mode-octahedral-rotation`）。SrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ では回転軸の方向に隣り合う八面体も "
"逆向きに回る。三つの方向すべてで隣の胞と逆になるので、凍結するのはR点のモードであり、 単位胞は "
":math:`\\sqrt2a\\times\\sqrt2a\\times2a` に大きくなる。この構造の空間群は :math:`I4/mcm` "
"である [ZhongVanderbilt1995]_ [HowardStokes1998]_。"
msgstr ""
"Adjacent octahedra share oxygen atoms at their corners, so when one "
"octahedron rotates, its neighbors in the same plane rotate in the "
"opposite direction (:numref:`fig-soft-mode-octahedral-rotation`). In "
"SrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , neighboring octahedra along the rotation axis also "
"rotate in opposite directions. The rotation reverses between neighboring "
"cells in all three directions, so the mode that freezes in is at R and "
"the unit cell expands to :math:`\\sqrt2a\\times\\sqrt2a\\times2a`. The "
"resulting structure has space group :math:`I4/mcm` [ZhongVanderbilt1995]_"
" [HowardStokes1998]_."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:323
msgid "回転軸の方向から見た頂点共有の八面体の網目。左の立方晶では正方形が45度傾いて並ぶ。右では八面体が交互に逆向きに回り、ルート2倍の新しい単位胞が破線で示される。"
msgstr ""
"Network of corner-sharing octahedra viewed along the rotation axis. Left:"
" The squares in the cubic phase are tilted by 45 degrees. Right: "
"Neighboring octahedra rotate in opposite directions. A dashed outline "
"marks the new unit cell, enlarged by a factor of √2."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:329
msgid ""
"回転軸の方向から見たTiO\\ :sub:`6`\\ 八面体の網目（Srは省略）。青丸がTi、赤丸が赤道面のO、 "
"薄い四角形が八面体の投影である。左は立方晶で、黒の正方形が元の単位胞の断面。右は回転角を誇張した図で、 ＋と−は回転の向き、緑の破線は面内で "
":math:`\\sqrt2` 倍になった単位胞の断面を示す。"
msgstr ""
"Network of TiO\\ :sub:`6`\\  octahedra viewed along the rotation axis (Sr"
" is omitted). Blue circles mark Ti, red circles mark O in the equatorial "
"plane, and the pale quadrilaterals are projections of the octahedra. "
"Left: The cubic phase, with a black square marking the cross section of "
"the original unit cell. Right: The rotation is exaggerated. The + and − "
"signs indicate the directions of rotation, and the dashed green outline "
"marks the cross section of the unit cell enlarged by a factor of "
":math:`\\sqrt2` in the plane."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:333
msgid ""
"八面体の回転は、各八面体の中心を動かさず、正負の電荷の重心もずらさないので、分極を生まない。 秩序変数は回転角 :math:`\\phi` "
"で、隣の胞へ一つ並進すると :math:`\\phi` が :math:`-\\phi` になるので、 :ref:`ゾーン境界のモードの等価性"
"<sm-inversion-equivalence>`\\ から :math:`E(\\phi)=E(-\\phi)` "
"である。ZhongとVanderbiltは、R点の回転モードに沿ったfrozen phonon計算（LDA）で、回転に対する曲率 "
":math:`\\kappa_R=\\frac12\\partial^2E/\\partial\\phi^2` "
"を8種類のペロブスカイトについて求めた。:math:`\\kappa_R<0` の物質は、この回転に対して不安定である "
"[ZhongVanderbilt1995]_。"
msgstr ""
"Octahedral rotation neither moves the centers of the octahedra nor shifts"
" the centroids of the positive and negative charge distributions, so it "
"produces no polarization. The order parameter is the rotation angle "
":math:`\\phi`. A translation to an adjacent cell takes :math:`\\phi` to "
":math:`-\\phi`, so the :ref:`equivalence for zone-boundary modes <sm-"
"inversion-equivalence>`\\  gives :math:`E(\\phi)=E(-\\phi)`. Zhong and "
"Vanderbilt used frozen phonon calculations (LDA) along the R-point "
"rotation mode to obtain the curvature with respect to rotation, "
":math:`\\kappa_R=\\frac12\\partial^2E/\\partial\\phi^2`, for eight "
"perovskites. Materials with :math:`\\kappa_R<0` are unstable against this"
" rotation [ZhongVanderbilt1995]_."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:337
msgid ""
"SrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ では、Γ点の極性モードも冷やすと低くなる [Cowley1964]_。それでも、最低温度まで強誘電相には "
"移らない。誘電率は低温で大きな値に飽和し、MüllerとBurkardはこれを量子常誘電と呼んだ [MullerBurkard1979]_。 "
"原子核の\\ :ref:`零点振動<zero-point-vibration>`\\ が、浅い井戸への秩序化を妨げるためである。 "
"このように、一つの物質に極性と非極性のソフトモードが共存し、一方の不安定性が他方を抑えることもある [ZhongVanderbilt1995]_。"
msgstr ""
"In SrTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , the polar Γ-point mode also softens on cooling "
"[Cowley1964]_. Even so, no ferroelectric phase appears down to the lowest"
" temperatures. The permittivity saturates at a large value at low "
"temperature, and Müller and Burkard called this quantum paraelectricity "
"[MullerBurkard1979]_. This occurs because nuclear \\ :ref:`zero-point "
"vibrations <zero-point-vibration>`\\  prevent ordering in the shallow "
"wells. A material can thus have both polar and nonpolar soft modes, and "
"one instability can suppress the other [ZhongVanderbilt1995]_."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:344
msgid "説明用の事例：BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の極性ソフトモード"
msgstr "Worked Example: Polar Soft Mode in BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ "

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:346
msgid ""
"BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ の立方晶相では、Γ点の極性モードがソフトモードであり、Harada、Axe、Shiraneが中性子散乱で "
"観測した [Harada1971]_。0 Kの第一原理計算では、このモードは\\ :ref:`虚数振動数<imaginary-"
"frequency>`\\ をもつ [CohenKrakauer1990]_。"
msgstr ""
"In the cubic phase of BaTiO\\ :sub:`3`\\ , the polar Γ-point mode is a "
"soft mode. Harada, Axe, and Shirane observed it by neutron scattering "
"[Harada1971]_. In first-principles calculations at 0 K, this mode has an "
"\\ :ref:`imaginary frequency <imaginary-frequency>`\\  (see "
"[CohenKrakauer1990]_)."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:349
msgid ""
"`計算事例「二重井戸ポテンシャル Part 2」 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/total-energy.html>`_\\ "
"は、5原子の立方晶セルを出発点に、CohenとKrakauerが求めた不安定モードの固有ベクトルの比でBa・Ti・Oを動かし、各変位で原子とセルを固定したOpenMX（LDA）の単点計算を行っている。"
" これは本稿のfrozen phonon法の手順にあたる。事例ではBaを固定したパターンを使っているが、 "
"井戸の深さを求めるだけなら、この固定は結果を変えない。"
msgstr ""
"The `calculation example “Double-Well Potential, Part 2” <https://example"
".quloud-platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/total-energy.html>`_\\  starts from a "
"cubic cell with five atoms. It displaces Ba, Ti, and O in the ratios of "
"the unstable-mode eigenvector obtained by Cohen and Krakauer, and "
"performs an OpenMX (LDA) single-point calculation at each displacement "
"with the atoms and cell fixed. This follows the procedure for the frozen "
"phonon method described here. The example uses a pattern with Ba fixed, "
"but holding Ba fixed does not affect the result if the goal is only to "
"determine the well depth."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:353
msgid ""
"同じ体積の :math:`Q=0` を基準にすると、立方晶の格子で〈001〉方向にも〈111〉方向にも二重井戸が現れ、 :math:`\\pm "
"Q` の二つの極小は反対向きの分極をもつ。〈111〉方向の井戸のほうが深いことは、4次までの模型 :eq:`sm-cubic-quartic` "
"では :math:`\\beta'<0` に対応する。正方晶のひずみを加えると〈001〉方向の井戸が深くなり、 :eq:`sm-strain` で"
" :math:`\\lambda\\eta<0` となる向きのひずみにあたる。体積を小さくすると両方の井戸が浅くなる。 "
"事例では、これらの傾向がCohenとKrakauerの報告と一致するとしている。変位の比や井戸の深さの数値は、 計算条件とともに事例に載っている。"
msgstr ""
"Relative to the energy at :math:`Q=0` at the same volume, the energy "
"curves show double wells along both 〈001〉 and 〈111〉 in the cubic lattice,"
" and the two minima at :math:`\\pm Q` have opposite polarizations. In the"
" expansion through fourth order (Equation :eq:`sm-cubic-quartic`), the "
"deeper well along 〈111〉 corresponds to :math:`\\beta'<0`. Applying "
"tetragonal strain deepens the 〈001〉 well, corresponding to strain in "
"Equation :eq:`sm-strain` with :math:`\\lambda\\eta<0`. Reducing the "
"volume makes both wells shallower. The example identifies these trends as"
" consistent with the results of Cohen and Krakauer. The displacement "
"ratios and numerical well depths are given in the example along with the "
"calculation conditions."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:359
msgid ""
"`計算事例「二重井戸ポテンシャル Part 1」 <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.html>`_\\ "
"は、Tiだけを〈001〉方向に動かした断面を、OpenMXと3種類の\\ :ref:`機械学習原子間ポテンシャル<mlip>`\\ "
"で比べている。Tiだけの変位は固有ベクトルではないが、この断面にも二重井戸が現れる。事例では、小さい変位での負の曲率を "
"再現するモデルと、大きい変位での壁をDFTに近く再現するモデルが一致しなかった。これは :ref:`二重井戸ポテンシャル<double-well-"
"potential>`\\ で述べたとおり、曲率と壁を別々に評価する必要がある例である。 事例は、高温の\\ :ref:`常誘電相"
"<paraelectric-phase>`\\ でも平均構造は立方晶のまま、瞬間的にはTiが中心からずれて局所的な極性をもちうると 述べている。"
msgstr ""
"The `calculation example “Double-Well Potential, Part 1” <https://example"
".quloud-platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/total-energy-DFT-MLIP.html>`_\\  uses "
"OpenMX and three kinds of \\ :ref:`machine learning interatomic "
"potentials <mlip>`\\  to compare the energy cross section obtained by "
"moving only Ti along 〈001〉. Displacing only Ti does not follow the "
"eigenvector, but this cross section also contains a double well. The "
"model that reproduced the negative curvature at small displacements was "
"different from the one whose walls at large displacements were close to "
"the DFT result. As discussed for the :ref:`double-well potential <double-"
"well-potential>`\\ , this is an example of why the curvature and the "
"walls must be assessed separately. The example states that even in the "
"high-temperature \\ :ref:`paraelectric phase <paraelectric-phase>`\\ , "
"the average structure remains cubic, but Ti can momentarily move off "
"center and produce local polarity."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:365
msgid ""
"有限温度の相転移の型については、Zhong、Vanderbilt、Rabeが第一原理計算からパラメータを決めた有効ハミルトニアンを "
"モンテカルロ法で解いた [Zhong1994]_ "
"[Zhong1995]_。立方晶相の転移温度のすぐ上で、各胞の局所的な変位の分布は弱く二つの山をもち、 "
"不安定な揺らぎはΓ点からX点への方向にゾーン境界まで広がっていた。上の\\ :ref:`判定の基準<displacive-order-"
"disorder>`\\ に従い、 彼らは立方晶–正方晶転移を、変位型と秩序–無秩序型の中間で、やや秩序–無秩序型に近いと結論した。 "
"X線の散漫散乱から提案されたTiの変位の鎖状の相関 [Comes1968]_ もこの結論と整合し、X線吸収微細構造でも、 "
"変位型と秩序–無秩序型の成分が共存すると報告されている [Stern2004]_。 相の順序と転移温度の計算値、揺らぎが鎖状に広がる理由は、「\\"
" :ref:`ferroelectric-origin`\\ 」の \\ :ref:`有限温度の計算<fo-finite-"
"temperature>`\\ で扱う。"
msgstr ""
"To study the type of phase transition at finite temperature, Zhong, "
"Vanderbilt, and Rabe used Monte Carlo to solve an effective Hamiltonian "
"parameterized from first-principles calculations [Zhong1994]_ "
"[Zhong1995]_. Just above the transition temperature of the cubic phase, "
"the distribution of local displacements in each cell was weakly bimodal, "
"and unstable fluctuations extended from the Γ point toward X as far as "
"the zone boundary. Using the \\ :ref:`criteria above <displacive-order-"
"disorder>`\\ , they concluded that the cubic-to-tetragonal transition "
"lies between the displacive and order–disorder limits and is slightly "
"closer to the order–disorder limit. The chain-like correlations of Ti "
"displacements proposed on the basis of diffuse X-ray scattering "
"[Comes1968]_ are consistent with this conclusion. X-ray absorption fine "
"structure has also been reported to show coexisting displacive and "
"order–disorder components [Stern2004]_. The calculated phase sequence and"
" transition temperatures, and the reason for the chain-like extent of the"
" fluctuations, are covered in “\\ :ref:`Origin of the Ferroelectric "
"Instability of BaTiO₃ <ferroelectric-origin>`\\ ”, in the section on \\ "
":ref:`finite-temperature calculations <fo-finite-temperature>`\\ ."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:375
msgid "解釈と限界"
msgstr "Interpretation and Limitations"

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:377
msgid ""
"0 Kの計算で高温相の構造に虚数振動数が出ることは、その近似のもとで高温相の構造が局所的に不安定で "
"あることを示す。転移温度や低温相の順序までは決まらない。 `計算事例「二重井戸ポテンシャル Part 2」の有限温度MD計算への接続 "
"<https://example.quloud-platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/total-"
"energy.html#md>`_\\ でも述べられているように、 二重井戸は0 "
"Kでの局所的なエネルギー面であり、有限温度の相転移には、胞どうしの変位の相関、格子のひずみ、 "
"エントロピー、熱揺らぎが加わる。これらを扱うには、\\ :ref:`分子動力学法<molecular-dynamics>`\\ "
"やモンテカルロ法などの統計的な計算が要る。"
msgstr ""
"An imaginary frequency in a 0 K calculation of the high-temperature "
"structure shows that the structure is locally unstable under that "
"approximation. It does not determine the transition temperature or the "
"sequence of low-temperature phases. As discussed in `the section on "
"connecting to finite-temperature MD calculations in the calculation "
"example “Double-Well Potential, Part 2” <https://example.quloud-"
"platform.quemix.com/BaTiO3/total-energy.html#md>`_\\ , the double well is"
" a local energy surface at 0 K. Finite-temperature phase transitions also"
" involve correlations between the displacements in different cells, "
"lattice strain, entropy, and thermal fluctuations. Treating these effects"
" requires statistical calculations such as \\ :ref:`molecular dynamics "
"<molecular-dynamics>`\\  or Monte Carlo."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:383
msgid ""
":math:`\\kappa` は体積に敏感なので、二重井戸の深さは計算に使う格子定数に強く依存する。\\ :ref:`交換相関汎関数"
"<exchange-correlation-functional>`\\ によって "
"平衡格子定数が変わると、井戸の深さや、不安定性が現れるかどうかまで変わりうる。異なる計算の井戸の深さを "
"比べるときは、体積をそろえるか、体積の違いを分けて考える必要がある。"
msgstr ""
"Because :math:`\\kappa` is sensitive to volume, the well depth depends "
"strongly on the lattice constant used in the calculation. A change in "
"equilibrium lattice constant due to the \\ :ref:`exchange-correlation "
"functional <exchange-correlation-functional>`\\  can alter the well depth"
" and even whether the instability appears. When comparing well depths "
"from different calculations, either use the same volume or consider the "
"effect of the volume difference separately."

#: ../../solid/soft_mode.rst:387
msgid ""
"ソフトモードの描像は、転移の前後で同じ原子配置の連続的な変形がたどれる場合に使える。原子の大きな再配列を "
"伴う転移や、秩序–無秩序型の極限では、振動数が0に近づくモードが観測されないこともある。"
msgstr ""
"The soft-mode picture applies when the atomic configuration can be "
"continuously deformed from one side of the transition to the other. A "
"mode whose frequency approaches zero may go unobserved in transitions "
"that involve large atomic rearrangements or in the order–disorder limit."

